comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T12:46:10.991Z",codex-sol,"Published reproduction: ran the issue public API snippet unchanged against official pm-gantt-chart@2026.10.10 with @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.12 and Node 24.19.0. related starts both items October 12; blocked_by correctly starts a October 13 after b October 12. implements incorrectly delays a to October 13; blocks incorrectly has the same direction as blocked_by. Equivalent a blocks b / b blocked_by a reports a false two-node cycle. Tarball npm receipt: SHA-1 c1edd221be472075eac8b169d22e339b5ba61cea. Import search found no existing owner; pm-github has no number/limit filter, so a gated atomic timestamp-filtered preview and import each selected exactly issue 135, with gh:unbraind/pm-gantt-chart#135 provenance. No other issues imported."
  "2026-10-12T12:54:25.680Z",codex-sol,"Design: replace the denylist with one normalized item-to-prerequisite graph using the active SDK relationship registry ordering flag and precedence. Deduplicate inverse and provenance-distinct constraints; preserve original item relationships in memory and all tracker/history bytes. Scheduling, cycles, critical path, slack and CSV/JSON exports consume the graph. Missing kinds retain legacy blocked_by behavior; unknown kinds remain contextual. Raise peer/manifest minimum to verified 2026.10.6 so registry APIs are enforced at activation; preserve closed pm-gantt-chart-k8wm ownership and its related-link behavior. Add real SDK-created tracker and installed-tarball CLI coverage plus custom kind registration and mixed-direction API corpora."
  "2026-10-12T12:57:39.368Z",codex-sol,"Installed published CLI reproduction completed: independent two-item Task/Decision scratch trackers created through the public SDK, both estimated_minutes=480; ran the exact scheduled JSON export command three separate times per scenario (18 total). related and blocked_by controls pass; implements delays a incorrectly; blocks incorrectly delays a rather than b; equivalent inverse rows falsely exit 2 with zero stdout and no output; a genuine blocked_by cycle still exits 2. Durable tracker, history and installed-package hashes remain unchanged by exports. The initial fixture used an unrecognized estimate option; corrected via the typed estimatedMinutes SDK field before recording these final results."
  "2026-10-12T13:22:34.208Z",codex-sol,"Custom-kind integration findings: PM SDK 2026.10.6 activates and publishes registered custom relationship kinds, but native create/update dependency input still rejects those names against a built-in-only allowed list. Also, package-local registry resolution and the injected client contracts read omit active custom definitions in an installed extension. Reproduced through real scratch projects; do not change upstream here. Gantt resolves an explicit workspace SDK client, gets the authoritative registered ordering census, and supplements built-in constraints using full one-hop native predecessor queries for custom ordering kinds. Synthetic custom CLI fixtures explicitly seed registered storage spellings and restore setup bytes afterward; exports themselves remain observational. No migrations or relabeling are added to package behavior."
  "2026-10-12T13:26:33.631Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: restored only the original bodies of computeCriticalPath, detectCycles, dataSanityReport, runDataSanityGate, computeSchedule, computeSlack, buildRows, renderCsv and renderJson, plus their original denylist helpers. Kept all new regression tests, registry adapter, package metadata and compatibility bounds unchanged. npm run build succeeded before node --test test/registry-ordering.test.ts. The reverted implementation exited 1: 9 tests, 2 pass, 7 fail, 0 skipped/canceled/todo. Failures are behavioral assertions for implements, recurs_from, incident_from, unknown context kinds, blocks direction, custom/mixed-direction ordering and the installed CLI. Related and genuine-cycle controls still pass. Restored the fix byte-for-byte and rebuilt dist before final validation."
  "2026-10-12T13:29:14.456Z",codex-sol,"Restored regression and linked evidence: npm run build && node --test test/registry-ordering.test.ts passes 9/9, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, with 12 installed CLI corpora plus equivalent source command/exporter assertions and durable-byte snapshots. pm test pm-gantt-chart-github-072477cd0a70-135 --run --progress --workspace-context snapshot also passes 9/9. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled, so the runner stores no automatic receipt; this comment records the observed result without changing project settings. Set the linked test to pm_context_mode=none with workspace_context_mode=snapshot: none/source was correctly refused before execution. The first restored clean-identity npm gate passes 241/241 and unchanged 100% lines/branches/functions for the configured index.ts runtime coverage scope; remaining release steps continue."
  "2026-10-12T13:34:51.301Z",codex-sol,"First Bun run: all 241 tests pass, but unchanged branch threshold fails at 99.38%. LCOV identifies five inherited buildRows fallback arms for missing schedule/slack entries. Those entries cannot be absent: both passes populate every working item before row construction, including cycle-guarded direct API calls. Remove only these unreachable lookups in the already-changed row builder and retain all thresholds. The final linked pm test command now uses stored snapshot workspace metadata and passes 9/9 without run-level overrides."
  "2026-10-12T13:45:36.881Z",codex-sol,"Final implementation gates pass: clean-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 241/241 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. Configured index.ts runtime coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions at unchanged thresholds; duplication is 0%, production audit has zero vulnerabilities, and each gate passes all three real packed npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum scenarios on the verified 2026.10.6 host. Lint, typecheck, docstrings, release workflow/date/publish-attestation checks and changelog check pass. npm run changelog:full regenerated the unchanged release-aware changelog after pm writes. Own-item history verification succeeds. The tracker remains in progress; release the claim for orchestrator review. Custom registry lookup uses an explicit workspace client; no upstream package changes, migrations or relationship relabeling are included."
  "2026-10-13T12:31:33.925Z",codex-agent,"Review fix round: verify registered ordering behavior, add real-tracker regression coverage and behavioral revert proof, merge the current base, rebuild committed dist, and run npm and Bun release gates. Review threads and bots will not be contacted."
  "2026-10-13T12:39:10.486Z",codex-agent,"Both findings are valid. Missing relationship_kind_contracts now selects zero custom definitions and retains built-in ordering. The pinned SDK graph signature accepts one id/target and exposes no multi-root predecessor batch, so queries use bounded batches of four and merge results in corpus order. All roots remain necessary for incoming source-before-target constraints; filtering only stored custom dependencies would lose successor prerequisites. Real-tracker coverage includes an omitted census, more than four roots, incoming custom constraints and self-cycles; instrumentation forwards real graph calls unchanged to verify overlap and the concurrency limit. Current origin/main is already incorporated."
  "2026-10-13T12:46:38.432Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed with unchanged regression tests and rebuilt dist. Reverting only customOrderingContracts fallback: focused tests 1 pass/1 fail, omitted census raises TypeError reading filter. Restoring that function and reverting only commandPrerequisiteGraph: 1 pass/1 fail, real graph concurrency drops from expected four to one. Restored both fixes and rebuilt. The focused baseline was 2/2; the existing real installed/source registry suite also passed 10/10 during this round."
  "2026-10-13T13:37:24.731Z",codex-agent,"Final clean-identity gates passed at unchanged thresholds. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 243 tests, 243 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, 0 skipped and 0 todo. Configured index.ts runtime coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions. Duplication is 0% (0/9549 lines, 28 sources, threshold 0%). Production audit found 0 vulnerabilities. Packed acceptance passed the npm-current, bun-current and npm-minimum scenarios on the pinned 2026.10.6 host. Lint, typecheck, docstrings, release workflow, changelog check, changelog-date and publish-attestation checks passed. The Bun command runs the repository gate chain; the test suite executes under Node. Focused regressions passed 2/2 after restore. Separate behavioral reverts: removing only the omitted-census fallback failed with a TypeError; restoring only the previous commandPrerequisiteGraph failed because observed peak concurrency was 1 rather than 4. Inherited development-audit high alerts in braces, micromatch, fast-glob and pm-ops stay owned by open pm-gantt-chart-e7rd; pins and thresholds were not changed. Item remains in_progress."
