close_reason: "Delivered by #136 \"fix: use registry ordering semantics for Gantt schedules\" (merged as 5dfa181). Checks successful at the PR head 7533d23: CodeQL, codeql, test (22.18.0), test (26)."
body: "## Published reproduction and scope\n\nThis is a compatibility/semantic improvement to the package's intentional denylist design, **not a regression claim about the earlier symmetric-related fix**.\n\nTested official `pm-gantt-chart@2026.10.10`, npm gitHead/current main `1838ce4f2ea2aaf50858e7d36d9fb5e480cffc9b`, with installed `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.12`, Node 24.19.0, Linux. Downloaded artifact matches npm SHA-1 and SHA-512. All examples use synthetic items; no service, model, or provider calls.\n\nThe host's [dependency-kind contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/docs/DEPENDENCY_KIND_CONTRACT.md) defines `A --blocks--> B` as B waiting for A, inverse to `B --blocked_by--> A`; implementation/association/provenance are distinct from ordering. Gantt instead treats every kind absent from its denylist as an item-to-prerequisite edge.\n\n## Minimal public API reproduction\n\n```js\nimport { computeSchedule, detectCycles } from \"pm-gantt-chart\";\nconst item = (id, dependencies = []) => ({\n  id, title: id, type: \"Task\", status: \"open\",\n  estimated_minutes: 480, dependencies\n});\nfor (const kind of [\"related\", \"implements\", \"blocked_by\", \"blocks\"]) {\n  const rows = [item(\"a\", [{ id: \"b\", kind }]), item(\"b\")];\n  console.log(kind, Object.fromEntries(\n    computeSchedule(rows, new Date(\"2026-10-12T00:00:00Z\"), 1)\n  ));\n}\nconsole.log(detectCycles([\n  item(\"a\", [{ id: \"b\", kind: \"blocks\" }]),\n  item(\"b\", [{ id: \"a\", kind: \"blocked_by\" }])\n]));\n```\n\nActual starts:\n- `related`: A Oct 12, B Oct 12 (passing non-ordering control)\n- `blocked_by`: A Oct 13, B Oct 12 (passing ordering control)\n- `implements`: A Oct 13, B Oct 12; expected neither ordered by this edge\n- `blocks`: A Oct 13, B Oct 12; expected A Oct 12, B Oct 13\n- Equivalent inverse rows return a two-node cycle, although they express the same single ordering constraint\n\nAdditional API probes show `recurs_from` and `incident_from` also order work under the current denylist. They were not exercised through the installed CLI.\n\n## Installed CLI confirmation and controls\n\nCreated independent two-item synthetic trackers through the current public SDK: Task `ga-a`, Decision `ga-b`, each estimated at 480 minutes. Installed the official package locally. On each tracker ran, in three separate processes:\n\n```sh\npm gantt export --format json --schedule --from 2026-10-12 --output chart.json\n```\n\nAll 18 executions were stable:\n- Related-only: exit 0; both starts Oct 12; no exported prerequisites\n- Implements-only: exit 0; ga-a starts Oct 13 and JSON reports `deps:[\"ga-b\"]`\n- Blocked-by-only: exit 0; ga-b Oct 12 then ga-a Oct 13\n- Blocks-only: exit 0; same wrong direction as blocked-by\n- Equivalent inverse rows: exit 2, zero stdout, no output file; falsely claims a fatal scheduling cycle\n- Genuine blocked-by cycle: exit 2, zero stdout, no output file (passing fail-closed control)\n\nPackage/tracker/history file hashes, excluding runtime files, stayed unchanged by the export runs. Successful JSON files were 1,281 bytes for related and 1,303 for the other single-edge cases. This is bounded semantic acceptance, not full-suite, cross-platform, performance, or agent-autonomy certification.\n\n## Existing ownership and requested direction\n\n[Closed pm-gantt-chart-k8wm](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/blob/1838ce4f2ea2aaf50858e7d36d9fb5e480cffc9b/.agents/pm/issues/pm-gantt-chart-k8wm.toon) / [PR #57](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/57) intentionally fixed known non-gating spellings while leaving the wider denylist design for a separate change/review. Its notes explicitly acknowledge implements/blocks still gate. Preserve that provenance and the passing related behavior.\n\nAll 97 canonical PM items and all 134 GitHub issue/PR records, open and closed, were checked October 12. No current matching open follow-up was found. [Context #136](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/issues/136) is related semantic work in a different package, not the Gantt owner.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Derive a normalized prerequisite graph from authoritative registry ordering semantics, including inverse direction; avoid another growing hard-coded denylist\n- Use that same graph for scheduling, cycle detection, critical path, slack, and exported prerequisites\n- Deduplicate equivalent forward/inverse constraints so they do not form a false cycle\n- Non-ordering association, implementation, provenance, and temporal links remain available as context without inventing dates or blocking chart generation\n- Test the cases above through public API and installed CLI, retain true-cycle fail-closed behavior, and add registered custom ordering/non-ordering kinds and mixed-direction corpora\n- Keep tracker data/history read-only; no implicit migration or relationship relabeling\n\nImpact: agents can receive invented sequencing, reversed schedules, or a refusal to render a valid tracker."
